{
  "comment": "Why: a haunted house is small rooms and sudden fright, not a hunt, so the table is lighter than the other evil roads (a budget of nine tenths, no roll bonus) and made of the things a house does: a cold spot, a rattling in the walls, armour that stands in the hall, doors that slam, a hag in the kitchen. The ghosts are vexes, which is the vanilla body that flies through walls; the noise gate is the slamming door, and the ambushes are the house waking all at once.",
